\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Now praise we great and famous
\par  work men,
\par The fathers, named in story;
\par And praise the Lord who now as then
\par Reveals in man His glory.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Praise we the wise and brave 
\par and strong,
\par Who graced their generation;
\par Who helped the right and fought 
\par the wrong,
\par And made our folk a nation.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Praise we the great of heart 
\par and mind,
\par The singers sweetly gifted,
\par Whose music like a migty Wind
\par The souls of men uplifted.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Praise we the peaceful men 
\par of skill
\par Who builded homes of beauty,
\par And, rich in art, made richer still
\par The brotherhood of duty.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Praise we the glorious names 
\par we know;
\par And they-whose names have perished,
\par Lost in the haze of long ago-
\par In silent love be cherished.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. In peace their sacred ashes rest,
\par Fulfilled their days endeavour;
\par They blest the earth, and they 
\par are blest
\par Of God and man, for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. So praise we great and famous men,
\par The fathers, named in story;
\par And praise the Lord who now as then
\par Reveals in man His glory.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

